.TH OMACHAT 1 "2026-08-31" "OmaChat 0.0.1"
.SH NAME
omachat \- OmaChat terminal client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B omachat
[\fB--socket\fR \fIPATH\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Opens the bounded ANSI terminal interface and connects to the per-user daemon.
Commands include /join, /leave, /who, /block, /send, /panic ERASE, and /detach.
Panic erasure is destructive and cannot remove copies already held by relays,
peers, backups, or filesystem snapshots.
.SH FILES
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/omachat/omachat.sock
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR omachat-ctl (1),
.BR omachatd (8),
.BR omachat-protocol (7)
